DEVICE DATA ATTRIBUTION

The device parameterizations in sim/jobs.py (screw layouts, removal
order, fastener specs, sourced-vs-UNSOURCED parameter lists) derive
from repair guides and teardowns published by iFixit:

  - iPhone 14 Pro Max battery replacement — iFixit guide 153006
  - iPhone 14 Pro Max rear camera replacement — iFixit guide 153334
  - Samsung Galaxy Note7 teardown — iFixit guide 66389
  - iPad Pro 11-inch (M1) battery replacement — iFixit guide 151810

iFixit publishes its guides under Creative Commons BY-NC-SA. Measured
facts taken from those guides (screw sizes, removal order) are cited
in sim/jobs.py with explicit sourced-vs-UNSOURCED lists; parameters
no source states are marked UNSOURCED there rather than invented.
This NOTICE is the attribution for that derived data.

SAMPLE RESULTS

The scorecards and transcripts under results/ are published as sample
results of the benchmark's first live runs, so that other benchmarkers
can see exactly what a PhoneBench run produces and what its reporting
looks like. They are covered by the same Apache-2.0 license as the
code; the live transcripts are gzip-compressed JSONL under
results/samples/.

Product names (iPhone, iPad, Samsung Galaxy Note7, Apple part numbers)
are used descriptively, to identify the devices the simulated jobs are
parameterized from. No affiliation with or endorsement by Apple,
Samsung, or iFixit is claimed.
